<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Monongahela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1755</span> · Also known as Braddock's Defeat · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Monongahela was fought on 9 July 1755 near the Monongahela River, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-duquesne">Fort Duquesne</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>. A British and colonial army under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-braddock">Edward Braddock</a>, marching to take the fort, was ambushed by a smaller force of French troops and Native allies and lost about two-thirds of its men, and Braddock was mortally wounded. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> helped lead the retreat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-monongahela.jpg" alt="Battle of the Monongahela" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacques Auguste Regnier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Washington_the_soldier.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
